From 1bc1179f7d31fb2b3f27bd79ea37d070946edbf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:14:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 006/344] FROMGIT: arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp: remove GPI DMA
 channel masks

It seems that different device may have different allowed GPI
interfaces (e.g. Microsoft Surface 9 5G's gpi_dma2 mask is 0x23 while
Huawei Matebook E Go 2023's gpi_dma2 mask is 0xb).

Remove the channel masks from the SoC DTSI file.

Signed-off-by: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260602081451.3808833-7-zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

(cherry picked from commit db4ac552889f6a952de872ea6128e1caca07fffb
 https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/qcom/linux.git for-next)
Signed-off-by: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
index fbcfd3883bbb4..975590a318ff2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
@@ -885,7 +885,6 @@ gpi_dma2: dma-controller@800000 {
 				     <GIC_SPI 599 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 			dma-channels = <12>;
-			dma-channel-mask = <0xfff>;
 			#dma-cells = <3>;
 
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0xb6 0x0>;
@@ -1311,7 +1310,6 @@ gpi_dma0: dma-controller@900000 {
 				     <GIC_SPI 256 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 			dma-channels = <13>;
-			dma-channel-mask = <0x1fff>;
 			#dma-cells = <3>;
 
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x576 0x0>;
@@ -1718,7 +1716,6 @@ gpi_dma1: dma-controller@a00000 {
 				     <GIC_SPI 298 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 			dma-channels = <12>;
-			dma-channel-mask = <0xfff>;
 			#dma-cells = <3>;
 
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x96 0x0>;
-- 
